        351.205078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "I. INTRODUCTION",
      "bbox": [
        135.61900329589844,
        374.146484375,
        213.37179565429688,
        383.05303955078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "N",
      "bbox": [
        48.96400451660156,
        391.23138427734375,
        70.21773529052734,
        417.6955261230469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ONLINEAR model predictive control (NMPC) has",
      "bbox": [
        71.71200561523438,
        391.6374816894531,
        300.02496337890625,
        400.5440368652344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "proven to be a powerful approach for controlling high-",
      "bbox": [
        71.71200561523438,
        403.59246826171875,
        300.0248107910156,
        412.4990234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "dimensional, complex robotic systems (e.g., [1], [2], [3],",
      "bbox": [
        48.96400451660156,
        415.5484619140625,
        300.021484375,
        424.45501708984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "[4]). Nevertheless, although these methods can handle large",
      "bbox": [
        48.96400451660156,
        427.5034484863281,
        300.0215148925781,
        436.4100036621094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "state spaces, nonlinear dynamics, and system constraints, their",
      "bbox": [
        48.96400451660156,
        439.45843505859375,
        300.021484375,
        448.364990234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "performance can be adversely affected by the presence of",
      "bbox": [
        48.96400451660156,
        451.4134216308594,
        300.02154541015625,
        460.3199768066406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "uncertainty even in the context of real-time replanning [5].",
      "bbox": [
        48.96400451660156,
        463.368408203125,
        300.0215148925781,
        472.27496337890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A number of approaches have been proposed to compensate",
      "bbox": [
        48.96400451660156,
        475.3233947753906,
        300.0215148925781,
        484.2299499511719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for this marginal robustness, the simplest of which is to",
      "bbox": [
        48.96400451660156,
        487.2793884277344,
        300.021484375,
        496.1859436035156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "generate a feedback policy to track the current receding-",
      "bbox": [
        48.96400451660156,
        499.234375,
        300.021484375,
        508.14093017578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "horizon plan (e.g., [2]). These approaches, however, do not",
      "bbox": [
        48.96400451660156,
        511.1893310546875,
        300.0214538574219,
        520.0958862304688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "account for uncertainty or closed-loop performance during the",
      "bbox": [
        48.96400451660156,
        523.1443481445312,
        300.0214538574219,
        532.0509033203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "planning process. To address this, approaches such as robust",
      "bbox": [
        48.96400451660156,
        535.099365234375,
        300.0215148925781,
        544.0059204101562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "NMPC (RNMPC) and stochastic NMPC (SNMPC) attempt",
      "bbox": [
        48.96400451660156,
        547.0543212890625,
        300.0215148925781,
        555.9608764648438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "to reason about the response of the policy to disturbances",
      "bbox": [
        48.96400451660156,
        559.0103759765625,
        300.0215148925781,
        567.9169311523438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "during planning. This is usually accomplished by making",
      "bbox": [
        48.96400451660156,
        570.96533203125,
        300.02154541015625,
        579.8718872070312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "simplifying assumptions about the dynamics and disturbances.",
      "bbox": [
        48.96400451660156,
        582.9203491210938,
        300.0215148925781,
        591.826904296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For instance, in RNMPC, disturbance sets may be approxi-",
      "bbox": [
        48.96400451660156,
        594.8753662109375,
        300.021484375,
        603.7819213867188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "mated by ellipsoids [6], or robustness guarantees may require",
      "bbox": [
        48.96400451660156,
        606.830322265625,
        300.0215148925781,
        615.7368774414062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the existence of a control contraction metric (CCM) [7]; in",
      "bbox": [
        48.96400451660156,
        618.7853393554688,
        300.0215148925781,
        627.69189453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
